12. AUTOMATIC DAILY AND PERIODIC UPDATES

The website must automatically retrieve new and updated flight information.

Implement a scheduled synchronization system.

Recommended architecture:

- Airport reference data: synchronize periodically according to the source's update schedule.
- Airline reference data: synchronize periodically.
- Flight schedules: synchronize ahead of the operating date and refresh regularly.
- Flight status: refresh more frequently for flights approaching departure or currently operating.
- Aircraft information: update when new verified information becomes available.

Use backend scheduled jobs or a reliable external scheduler.

Do not rely on a visitor opening the website to trigger synchronization.

Store the following:

- Last synchronization time.
- Last successful API request.
- Data source.
- Number of records imported.
- Number of records updated.
- Failed synchronization attempts.
- API quota usage.

Display:

"Last updated: [actual timestamp]"

Use appropriate caching to reduce unnecessary API calls.

Do not repeatedly fetch all worldwide records every few minutes.

Use incremental synchronization wherever possible.

Ensure that failed updates do not delete previously valid records.

Preserve historical flight information when permitted by the data provider's licensing terms.

